    "value": "15"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1965-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The leading terms force quotient \\(x+1.\\) Expanding, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(x+1)(x^3+3x^2+9x+3)\\\\ &\\quad=x^4+4x^3+12x^2+12x+3. \\end{aligned} \\] Thus \\(6p=12,\\ 4q=12,\\ r=3,\\) so \\(p=2,\\ q=3\\) and \\((p+q)r=15.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "The quotient must be monic and linear",
        "Subtract \\((x+1)(x^3+3x^2+9x+3)\\) and compare coefficients"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
